<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>There’s an outer part of me—</l><l>That’s my body—you can see,</l><l>But there’s more to me than this—</l><l>More than this, more than this.</l><l>Yes, my body’s where I live—</l><l>Like my house, I am inside,</l><l>Like the clothes that I may wear,</l><l>I’m inside! I’m inside!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Deeper than the part you see</l><l>Is my soul—yes, that is me!</l><l>And this soul has its own parts:</l><l>Mind and will! Feelings, too!</l><l>With my soul I feel and think,</l><l>With this soul my choices make,</l><l>With my soul I love and choose—</l><l>Love the Lord! Choose the Lord!</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Deep within this inner part</l><l>There’s a special part of me—</l><l>It’s my spirit—for the Lord!</l><l>Deepest part! For the Lord!</l><l>This one part just matches God—</l><l>Here my conscience speaks for Him,</l><l>It’s reserved just for the Lord—</l><l>Deepest part! For the Lord!</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>May your spirit and your soul</l><l>And your body be preserved,</l><l>Your whole being, sanctified</l><l>By our God! God of peace!</l><l>Without blame before the Lord,</l><l>Your whole being, till He comes,</l><l>Be kept blameless and so pure,</l><l>Be preserved! Be preserved!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
